{"title":"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following integers is closest to zero?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/96784a37b7d98b708046e049387985345705e2e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\  -1101\\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 1011\\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ -1010\\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ -1001\\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 1110$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"591\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We need to find the number that has the least distance to 0. To do this, we can take the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Absolute_value\" title=\"Absolute value\">absolute value</a> of each number, and see which number is the lowest:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/8/4f8f0d8455818ea120e1465aafed119dd1ec250e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|-1101| = 1101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/e/e9ecf93f66f44cbc829d5b9187af2430254634f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|1011| = 1011$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/e/06eb52e93c6a4943b01656ecd22d177c39240b77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|-1010| = 1010$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c941715eebad73ef08ee422a2a3b71cb2457a1a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|-1001| = 1001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/b/aebe1e1a2d951835841fe1f39ce13b7f968bbcf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|1110| = 1110$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>The smallest of these numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888c508062c09735bab7ff0e11e7dc80cc7580db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/4/9b45c2b577d26b6c8eccc9f7652dd2770f551eee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } -1001}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"108\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Pro